[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged **412 reports** as one issue and marked it known. Read by
tenant (locale and booking form), not by intake tag, they are three problems.

<Callout>
Not one issue. One fix queued covers only the largest of three.
</Callout>

## The three problems

| Problem | Reports | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| `parser` | 374 | The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get flipped dates. Affects all 11 tenants. |
| `hint` | 33 | `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so day-first people type month first. A form bug, not a parser bug. Affects alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour. |
| one-day move | 5 | The date is off by exactly one day, not by a month flip (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620). Looks like a time zone problem. Filed under `parser` by tenant. |

374 + 33 + 5 = 412.

## What the counts rest on

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

- The table puts the 5 one-day reports under `parser`; this page counts them on their own.
- The export repeats 15 reports across overlapping pages. One id is one report.
- Intake tags are wrong for 38 reports: 23 tagged `hint` are `parser`, 15 tagged `parser` are `hint`.
  Only the tenant's locale and form say which.

## Lessons

- Merging on subject alone (decision 0001) hid two problems inside one count.
- A fix for the parser will not fix `booking-v3` or the one-day move.

